{"id":"background-bash","path":"spec/capabilities/background-bash.yaml","doc":{"statement":"A shell command can be started in the background: the agent gets a receipt at once naming the task and the file its output goes to, and the command keeps running while the agent works.","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/tools-reference#background-commands"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgbash","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/midturn"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock does not model a background command's time limit: the docs give 30 minutes by default, or the timeout passed with run_in_background up to 2 hours (raised by BASH_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MS and BASH_MAX_TIMEOUT_MS), and a stop notice reading 'Background command \"<description>\" was stopped after reaching its background time limit'. A mock's background command runs until it ends or the session reaps it."},{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock does not model a foreground command moving to the background: the docs say one that reaches its timeout is moved to the background ('Command did not complete within its 120s timeout and was moved to the background', with the task id and output file), and that a foreground sub-agent's moved command still stops when that sub-agent's run ends. A mock's foreground command is never moved."}]},"codex":"pending","cursor":"pending"}}}
