{"id":"hook-exit-code-semantics","path":"spec/capabilities/hook-exit-code-semantics.yaml","doc":{"statement":"A hook command's exit status classifies its outcome: accepted (0), blocked (2, with the hook's stderr as its message when it gave no other reason), or a non-blocking error (any other status, except on WorktreeCreate, where any non-zero status fails the creation, and except, in a harness that reads a hook's output whatever its status, when stdout holds valid JSON, which alone decides the outcome), after which the action goes on, unless the harness has a setting that makes a hook's failures (a non-zero status, a crash, no output) block the action instead. What a block does on each event, how accepted output is used (context, decisions, updated input) and hook timeouts are those events' and hook output's own capabilities.","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#exit-code-output","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#exit-code-2-behavior-per-event","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#other-exit-codes"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-json","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/prompt-blocked","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/prompt-blocked-suppressed","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-unstartable","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock fires SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit, PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PostToolUseFailure, Stop, SubagentStart, SubagentStop, PreCompact, PostCompact, SessionEnd, WorktreeCreate and WorktreeRemove, and no others. The docs' exit-code rows for StopFailure (which the mock defines but never fires), ConfigChange, CwdChanged, DirectoryAdded, Elicitation, ElicitationResult, FileChanged, InstructionsLoaded, MessageDisplay, Notification, PermissionDenied, PermissionRequest, PostModelSwitch, PostToolBatch, PreModelSwitch, Setup, TaskCompleted, TaskCreated, TeammateIdle and UserPromptExpansion are not modeled."},{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"A hook's JSON that fails Claude Code's output schema is a non-blocking error in the mock too, whose message names the failing field and carries the hook's own stderr, but not the full output schema Claude Code prints after it. Only an invalid decision gives Claude Code's recorded wording; any other field's complaint is the mock's own."},{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"WorktreeRemove fails on a non-zero hook exit only if the worktree's directory still exists afterward. The mock's worktree_remove manages no directory, so any non-zero exit fails it."}]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#pretooluse","https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#userpromptsubmit","https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#posttooluse","https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#stop"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-json","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-unstartable","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/prompt-blocked","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/posttool-block","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock fires SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit, PreToolUse, PostToolUse and Stop, and no others. The docs' exit-code rows for PermissionRequest, PreCompact, PostCompact, SubagentStart, SubagentStop, Interrupt and SessionEnd are not modeled."}]},"cursor":{"docs":["https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#command-based-hooks","https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#per-script-configuration-options","https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#troubleshooting"],"runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes","cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-fail-closed","cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-json-nonzero","cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-refusal"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock fires sessionStart, sessionEnd, preToolUse, postToolUse, postToolUseFailure, beforeShellExecution, afterShellExecution and afterFileEdit, and no others. The docs' exit-code rules for the other permission hooks (beforeMCPExecution, beforeReadFile, beforeTabFileRead, subagentStart) and for afterMCPExecution, subagentStop, beforeSubmitPrompt, preCompact, stop, afterAgentResponse, afterAgentThought, the Tab hooks and workspaceOpen are not modeled; the recordings show cursor-agent in print mode firing none of beforeSubmitPrompt, afterAgentResponse and stop."}]}}}}
{"id":"hook-matcher-filter","path":"spec/capabilities/hook-matcher-filter.yaml","doc":{"statement":"Hooks are configured per event with an optional matcher, and a hook runs only for events whose subject (for tool events, the tool name) matches it. An event with no subject takes every hook, whatever its matcher. (A finer condition on a tool's arguments is not a matcher and is not part of this.)","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#matcher-patterns"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/matcher"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock defines only the events named in claude-mock/internal/hooks/event.go (SessionStart, SessionEnd, Stop, StopFailure, SubagentStart, SubagentStop, PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PostToolUseFailure, WorktreeCreate, WorktreeRemove, PreCompact, PostCompact, UserPromptSubmit), so the matcher rows of the docs' table for the other events (Notification, Setup, ConfigChange and the like) are not modeled."}]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#matcher-patterns"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-matchers"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock fires no PermissionRequest, PreCompact, PostCompact, SubagentStart or SubagentStop event and has no MCP tools or sub-agents, so the matcher variants of those (MCP tool names such as mcp__filesystem__.*, the manual|auto compaction triggers, the sub-agent types, and spawn_agent also matching Agent) are not modeled. The mock's tool-name aliases are only apply_patch matching Edit and Write."}]},"cursor":{"docs":["https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#matcher-configuration","https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#per-script-configuration-options"],"runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-matchers"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock fires only the events it fires (sessionStart, sessionEnd, preToolUse, postToolUse, postToolUseFailure, beforeShellExecution, afterShellExecution and afterFileEdit), so the matchers of the other events (subagentStart, subagentStop, beforeReadFile, beforeSubmitPrompt, stop, afterAgentResponse, afterAgentThought and the rest) are not modeled."}]}}}}
{"id":"hook-output-transcript-records","path":"spec/capabilities/hook-output-transcript-records.yaml","doc":{"statement":"What hooks do leaves records in the session transcript: a silent success leaves nothing, while errors, blocks, cancellations and the context a hook adds are recorded, and each stop that ran hooks ends with a summary record. (Where context too long to keep goes is hook-additional-context's, and a stop hook that gives context without blocking is not part of this.)","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#exit-code-0","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#other-exit-codes","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#add-context-for-claude"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookmix","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgbash","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout"]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#userpromptsubmit"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/posttool-block","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/prompt-blocked","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-decisions"],"deviations":[{"adr":"capability-grounding","statement":"Codex records less than the statement says: a hook that fails without blocking (exit 1, a failure at SessionStart) and a hook stopped by its timeout leave no record, a prompt a hook blocks leaves no record of the reason (runs/prompt-blocked), and the end of a turn that ran hooks gets no summary record (recorded: runs/hook-exit-codes, runs/hook-timeout). What it records is the context a hook adds (a developer message), a block of a tool call (that call's result) and the reason a stop hook blocks with (a hook_prompt user message), and the mock records just those."}]},"cursor":{"supported":false,"reason":"Cursor's transcript holds only user and assistant messages, so nothing a hook output, blocked, cancelled or added is recorded there.","runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes","cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/additional-context","cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout"]}}}}
{"id":"hook-timeout","path":"spec/capabilities/hook-timeout.yaml","doc":{"statement":"A hook is bounded by a timeout; when it expires, the hook and every process it spawned are killed, whatever it printed is discarded, and the event carries on. (How long a hook with no timeout of its own may run is the harness's default for the event. Hooks run in the background, and the handler kinds that are neither a command nor an endpoint, are not part of this.)","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#timeouts","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#common-fields"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock defines and fires none of the PreModelSwitch, PostModelSwitch and MessageDisplay events, so the shorter default timeouts the docs give them (30 s, 30 s and 10 s), and a timed-out PreModelSwitch hook blocking the model switch, are not modeled. The mcp_tool hook handler is not implemented either, so a timed-out mcp_tool hook's cancellation and discarded output are not modeled."},{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"A timed-out PreToolUse hook lets the call fall through to the normal permission flow. The mock models a non-interactive run with no permission rules evaluated beside the hook, so what a deny or ask rule does after a timeout is not modeled."}]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#config-shape"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"Codex also gives the Interrupt event a default of 1 second, capped at 3, but the mock fires no Interrupt event (a non-interactive run has nothing to interrupt), so that default is not modeled."}]},"cursor":{"docs":["https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#per-script-configuration-options"],"runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout"]}}}}
