{"id":"hook-timeout","path":"spec/capabilities/hook-timeout.yaml","doc":{"statement":"A hook is bounded by a timeout; when it expires, the hook and every process it spawned are killed, whatever it printed is discarded, and the event carries on. (How long a hook with no timeout of its own may run is the harness's default for the event. Hooks run in the background, and the handler kinds that are neither a command nor an endpoint, are not part of this.)","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#timeouts","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#common-fields"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock defines and fires none of the PreModelSwitch, PostModelSwitch and MessageDisplay events, so the shorter default timeouts the docs give them (30 s, 30 s and 10 s), and a timed-out PreModelSwitch hook blocking the model switch, are not modeled. The mcp_tool hook handler is not implemented either, so a timed-out mcp_tool hook's cancellation and discarded output are not modeled."},{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"A timed-out PreToolUse hook lets the call fall through to the normal permission flow. The mock models a non-interactive run with no permission rules evaluated beside the hook, so what a deny or ask rule does after a timeout is not modeled."}]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#config-shape"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"Codex also gives the Interrupt event a default of 1 second, capped at 3, but the mock fires no Interrupt event (a non-interactive run has nothing to interrupt), so that default is not modeled."}]},"cursor":{"docs":["https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#per-script-configuration-options"],"runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-timeout"]}}}}
{"id":"hooks-all-matching-run","path":"spec/capabilities/hooks-all-matching-run.yaml","doc":{"statement":"Every hook that matches an event runs, all together, even when one of them blocks; when several block, the harness acts on the one that finishes last or merges them. The same hook configured in several settings files runs once, in a harness that reads more than one. (How the decisions and the context of several hooks combine is each decision's and context's own capability.)","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#hook-handler-fields","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks-guide#combine-results-from-multiple-hooks"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/all-hooks","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/all-hooks-slow-first"]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#where-codex-looks-for-hooks","https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#pretooluse"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-decisions","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hooks-all-matching-run-blockers-slow-first","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hooks-all-matching-run-blockers-fast-first","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hooks-all-matching-run-same-hook-two-files"],"deviations":[{"adr":"capability-grounding","statement":"When several hooks block one call, Codex acts on neither the one that finishes last nor a merge: it acts on the first in configuration order, whichever finishes first, after all of them have run to completion (recorded: a slow and a fast hook that both deny, in either order, and the reason told is the first configured's), and the mock does the same."},{"adr":"capability-grounding","statement":"Codex does not run a hook configured in several settings files once: the same command in the user layer's and the project layer's hooks.json runs once per file, twice in all (recorded: runs/hooks-all-matching-run-same-hook-two-files), and the mock does the same."},{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock reads hooks only from the user's and the project's hooks.json: the inline [hooks] tables of config.toml (user and project), plugin-bundled hooks and managed hooks, which Codex also loads and runs beside them, are not modeled."}]},"cursor":{"docs":["https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#configuration"],"runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/hooks-together","cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-refusal"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock reads only the project's .cursor/hooks.json: the user, team and enterprise sources, and so a hook configured in more than one, are not modeled."}]}}}}
{"id":"http-hooks","path":"spec/capabilities/http-hooks.yaml","doc":{"statement":"A hook can be an HTTP endpoint that receives the event payload as the body of a POST. A 2xx answer whose body is a JSON object decides like a command's printed JSON; an empty 2xx body is a success; anything else (a non-2xx status, an endpoint that cannot be reached, a 2xx body that is not a JSON object) is a non-blocking error: no status alone blocks. (The request's headers and the lists of endpoints and variables an administrator allows are not part of this.)","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#http-hook-fields","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#http-response-handling"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/http-hook"]},"codex":{"supported":false,"reason":"Codex hook handlers are only command and mcp_tool (prompt and agent are skipped); there is no HTTP endpoint handler.","docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#config-shape"]},"cursor":{"supported":false,"reason":"Cursor hooks have two execution types, command-based and prompt-based; there is no HTTP endpoint hook.","docs":["https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#hook-types"]}}}}
{"id":"manual-compaction","path":"spec/capabilities/manual-compaction.yaml","doc":{"statement":"The session can be compacted on request; hooks fire before and after the compaction, and the hook before it can stop it.","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#precompact","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#postcompact"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/compact","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/compact-nohooks"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"/compact is a slash command, and no mock parses one: a scenario's compact control record requests the compaction, so PreCompact's custom_instructions is always null and the text a user passes after /compact is not modeled."},{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock has no API and no context window, so it never compacts by itself and never meets a context-limit error: an automatic compaction is requested by a scenario, and the variant where blocking an automatic compaction that was triggered to recover from a context-limit error surfaces that error is not modeled. A blocked automatic compaction is skipped and the conversation continues uncompacted."}]},"codex":"pending","cursor":"pending"}}}
{"id":"nested-subagents","path":"spec/capabilities/nested-subagents.yaml","doc":{"statement":"A sub-agent can itself dispatch sub-agents; each records its depth and its parent, and all of a session's sub-agent transcripts sit in one directory. Nesting stops at a depth limit (three layers by default, set by CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_SUBAGENT_SPAWN_DEPTH), where a dispatch is an error, and in non-interactive mode a sub-agent does not wait for the background sub-agents it launched.","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents#let-subagents-spawn-their-own-subagents"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/meta"]},"codex":"pending","cursor":"pending"}}}
{"id":"noninteractive-run","path":"spec/capabilities/noninteractive-run.yaml","doc":{"statement":"A single prompt can be run to completion without interaction, streaming one machine-readable event per record and ending with one result.","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference#cli-flags","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/headless#basic-usage","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/headless#stream-responses"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bashfail"]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/noninteractive#make-output-machine-readable"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/prompt-blocked"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock accepts -o/--output-last-message and does nothing with it: the final message is not written to a file. It calls no model and has no failing turn or stream failure, so the turn.failed event and the stream-level error event the docs name are not modeled. The stream's item types are the agent message and the command execution only: reasoning, file changes, MCP tool calls, web searches and plan updates are not modeled."}]},"cursor":{"docs":["https://cursor.com/docs/cli/headless#how-it-works","https://cursor.com/docs/cli/headless#real-time-progress-tracking"],"runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-refusal"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock models only the stream-json output format. The docs' default text format (the final answer only), the json format and --stream-partial-output (partial assistant text deltas as the agent writes) are not modeled: another --output-format is refused, and --stream-partial-output is accepted and ignored."}]}}}}
{"id":"plugin-hooks","path":"spec/capabilities/plugin-hooks.yaml","doc":{"statement":"Hooks contributed by enabled plugins, resolved through the marketplace the settings declare, run alongside the project's own hooks; an undeclared marketplace or disabled plugin contributes none. (Where a plugin's files are fetched from, beyond a directory on disk, is not part of this.)","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#hook-locations","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugin-marketplaces#add-plugin-entries"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/plugin-hooks"]},"codex":"pending","cursor":"pending"}}}
{"id":"posttooluse-payload","path":"spec/capabilities/posttooluse-payload.yaml","doc":{"statement":"After a tool call succeeds, a hook fires with the tool's input, its structured response and how long the call took. (What a particular tool's response contains is that tool's own capability's.)","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#posttooluse","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#posttooluse-input"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors"]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#posttooluse"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/posttool-block"],"deviations":[{"adr":"capability-grounding","statement":"Codex's PostToolUse payload does not say how long the call took: it has no duration field, in its doc or in any recorded payload, and the mock sends none."},{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock runs the shell tool and a sub-agent dispatch only, so what PostToolUse reports for apply_patch, MCP tool calls and other local function tools is not modeled."}]},"cursor":{"docs":["https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#posttooluse"],"runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/file-tools","cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/tool-failure","cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-refusal"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock runs the Shell, Read and Write tools only, so what the MCP tools' and the other tools' successful calls report to postToolUse is not modeled. It times a command, but reports a duration of 0 for a file tool's call."}]}}}}
{"id":"pretooluse-refusal","path":"spec/capabilities/pretooluse-refusal.yaml","doc":{"statement":"A PreToolUse hook can refuse a tool call before it runs, by denying it in its output or by blocking it with its exit status; the refusal reaches the agent as the tool's error result, the tool does not run, and the turn goes on. When several hooks decide one call, a deny wins over any other decision. (What exit statuses mean is hook-exit-code-semantics'; changing the tool's input or adding context are other capabilities'.)","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#pretooluse-decision-control","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#exit-code-2-behavior-per-event"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock models a non-interactive run that no SDK host resumes, so a hook's \"ask\" (a permission prompt) and \"defer\" (pausing the call to resume later) decide nothing in the mock; they only rank below deny when several hooks decide one call. Permission rules evaluated beside the hook are not modeled."}]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#pretooluse","https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#tool-coverage"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-decisions"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock's tool executor handles only the shell tool (hooks name it Bash), so a refusal of apply_patch, of MCP tools and of Codex's other local function tools is not modeled. Hosted tools such as web search run no hook in Codex either."}]},"cursor":{"docs":["https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#pretooluse","https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#beforeshellexecution--beforemcpexecution","https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#configuration"],"runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-refusal"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock models a non-interactive run with no one to ask, so a hook's \"ask\" (a permission prompt) decides nothing in the mock; it only ranks below deny when several hooks decide one call. The call-refusing hooks the mock fires are preToolUse and beforeShellExecution; beforeMCPExecution, beforeReadFile and subagentStart, which refuse too, are not modeled."},{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"A deny's agent_message, which the docs say is fed back to the agent as the refusal, is not read: the mock has no model to receive it, and the recorded stream shows the agent's side of a refusal only as the rejected tool call, so only the hook's user_message (the failure hook's error_message) is modeled."}]}}}}
{"id":"print-waits-for-background-agents","path":"spec/capabilities/print-waits-for-background-agents.yaml","doc":{"statement":"In a non-interactive run, the session stays open until its background sub- agents finish, and each one's completion starts a further turn.","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/headless#background-tasks-at-exit"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/bgagent"]},"codex":"pending","cursor":"pending"}}}
{"id":"schedule-wakeup","path":"spec/capabilities/schedule-wakeup.yaml","doc":{"statement":"The agent can ask to be woken after a delay with a prompt; a delay under a minute or over an hour is clamped to those limits, and the request is acknowledged with the time it is set for.","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/scheduled-tasks#let-claude-choose-the-interval"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/schedule-wakeup-limits"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock has no clock to wait on: a valid request is acknowledged and the turn goes on at once, as the wake-up having fired, so the harness's re-invocation when the wakeup fires or a task-notification arrives, and the jitter the recorded wake-up times show beyond rounding up to a whole minute, are not modeled. A self-paced /loop (a slash command, interactive surface) is what Claude calls this tool for; no mock parses one."}]},"codex":{"supported":false,"reason":"Codex exec offers the agent no wake-up or timer tool; asked to schedule one it searched its tools for a wake-up tool, found none, and made no scheduling call.","runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/schedule-wakeup-ask"]},"cursor":{"supported":false,"reason":"Cursor's wake-up timer tool (subscribe_timer) exists only for Cloud Agents; a local agent searched for it, found none and said it has no such tool.","runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/schedule-wakeup-ask"]}}}}
{"id":"session-end-hook","path":"spec/capabilities/session-end-hook.yaml","doc":{"statement":"A hook fires when the session ends and says why; a non-interactive run reports a generic reason. Whatever the hook prints is not recorded in the transcript. (How long it may run is hook-timeout's, and which reasons a configured matcher selects is hook-matcher-filter's.)","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#sessionend","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#sessionend-input"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The reasons clear, resume, logout and prompt_input_exit belong to an interactive session (/clear, /resume, a logout, an exit from the prompt). The mock models none, so every session ends with the generic reason."}]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#sessionend"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-end"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The docs name SessionEnd triggers of an app-managed thread: archiving or deleting it, and 30 minutes of idleness. The mock models a non-interactive run, which ends with its turn, so it fires SessionEnd for that only."},{"adr":"capability-grounding","statement":"That what the hook prints is not recorded in the transcript is not shown for Codex: the docs say only that SessionEnd hooks are advisory and their output does not steer Codex, and the recorded run's hook prints nothing. The mock does not record it."}]},"cursor":{"docs":["https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#sessionend"],"runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/pretool-refusal"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock has no interactive session, and models a run that ends by its script's result, so the sessionEnd reasons window_close, user_close, aborted and error, and the error message that goes with a reason of error, are not modeled: it always says completed."}]}}}}
{"id":"session-fork","path":"spec/capabilities/session-fork.yaml","doc":{"statement":"A session can be forked when resumed: the fork continues the conversation under a new session id in a new transcript that carries the history, and the original is left untouched.","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference#cli-flags","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/sessions#fork-to-explore-alternatives"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/forkresume"]},"codex":"pending","cursor":"pending"}}}
{"id":"session-resume-unknown","path":"spec/capabilities/session-resume-unknown.yaml","doc":{"statement":"Resuming a session that does not exist fails with a no-conversation message and a non-zero exit, after the end-of-session hook has fired and without a start hook.","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference#cli-flags","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/sessions#resume-by-id"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/resume-unknown"]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/noninteractive#resume-a-non-interactive-session"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-resume-unknown"],"deviations":[{"adr":"capability-grounding","statement":"Codex fails the resume before it starts any session, so no hook fires at all: the end-of-session hook the statement has does not fire (recorded: runs/session-resume-unknown, no hook payload at all), and the mock fires none either. The message is a no-rollout one on stderr, and the exit is 1."}]},"cursor":{"supported":false,"reason":"cursor-agent --resume with an unknown session id does not fail; it runs a new session under that id and exits 0.","runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/session-resume-unknown"]}}}}
{"id":"session-resume","path":"spec/capabilities/session-resume.yaml","doc":{"statement":"A session can be resumed by id: it continues in its existing transcript, even when resumed from another working directory, and a top-level resume fires session hooks but no sub-agent hooks.","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference#cli-flags","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/sessions#resume-by-id","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/headless#continue-conversations"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/forkresume","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/compact"]},"codex":"pending","cursor":"pending"}}}
{"id":"session-start-hook","path":"spec/capabilities/session-start-hook.yaml","doc":{"statement":"A hook fires when a session begins and, in a harness that starts a session in more than one way, says how it began: fresh, resumed, forked, or continuing after a compaction. The hook cannot stop the session from starting. (What else the hook receives or may return, such as context for the agent, is other capabilities'.)","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#sessionstart-input","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#sessionstart-decision-control","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#exit-code-2-behavior-per-event"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"A session cleared with /clear starts again with source \"clear\" in Claude Code. The mock parses no slash command, so it never reports that source."}]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#sessionstart"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes","codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-matchers"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock never resumes, forks or compacts a session, so a session start is always the fresh one, source startup."}]},"cursor":{"docs":["https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#sessionstart"],"runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/session-start-block","cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/symlinked-cwd"],"deviations":[{"adr":"modeled-surface","statement":"The mock never resumes, forks or compacts a conversation, so it fires one sessionStart hook per run, at the fresh start."}]}}}}
{"id":"session-transcript-file","path":"spec/capabilities/session-transcript-file.yaml","doc":{"statement":"Each session's transcript is a file under the configuration directory, keyed by the working directory with symlinks resolved and by the session id; a fresh session's file does not exist yet when the start hook runs.","providers":{"claude":{"docs":["https://code.claude.com/docs/en/claude-directory#application-data","https://code.claude.com/docs/en/env-vars#variables"],"runs":["claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/forkresume","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/hookerrors","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/symlinked-cwd","claude-mock/snapshots/runs/transcript-at-start"]},"codex":{"docs":["https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#common-input-fields"],"runs":["codex-mock/snapshots/runs/session-transcript-file"],"deviations":[{"adr":"capability-grounding","statement":"Codex does not key the transcript by working directory: its rollout file is <config dir>/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-<start time>-<session id>.jsonl, the day it started and the session id, and the working directory is only a field of the file's first record (recorded: runs/session-transcript-file). The mock does the same."},{"adr":"capability-grounding","statement":"Codex creates a fresh session's file before the start hook runs: the file the SessionStart payload's transcript_path names already exists then, and the mock does the same (recorded: runs/session-transcript-file)."}]},"cursor":{"docs":["https://cursor.com/docs/hooks#common-schema"],"runs":["cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/tool-failure","cursor-mock/snapshots/runs/symlinked-cwd"]}}}}
